; =====================================================================
; embedded-abnf.abnf
;
; VERBATIM.  Every region below is RFC 9165's own bytes, copied unchanged,
; with the RFC's three-column body margin and the figures' own extra
; indentation intact.  It was NOT authored by this project.  Do not edit it,
; do not correct it, do not reformat it.  Defects found in it are recorded in
; README.md, never repaired here.
;
; THIS FILE WILL NOT PARSE AS ABNF AS IT STANDS, and that is the point.
; RFC 5234 is line-oriented: an indented line is a continuation, so an
; indented rule-list collapses into one rule.  Removing that indentation is
; not a convenience here - it is what the .det control operator DOES
; (Section 2.3).  The companion that applies the document's own dedenting
; definition, and is therefore what a tool actually parses, is
; embedded-abnf-dedented.derived.abnf.
;
; What ABNF this document contains, and in what voice:
;   A-1  Section 3.  The document's OWN production, in its own voice, not an
;        example: it redefines RFC 5234's CRLF core rule.  See README.md.
;   A-2  Figure 3 / Figure 4.  The cbor-tags-oid rule-list, inside a CDDL
;        byte-string literal.
;   A-3  Figure 5.  The rfc3339 rule-list, from RFC 3339, inside a CDDL
;        byte-string literal.
;   A-4  Figure 5.  The rfc5234-core rule-list, which the document abbreviates
;        to DIGIT alone with the comment "; abbreviated here".
;
; A-3 AND A-4 ARE NOT ADJACENT IN THE SOURCE.  Source lines 341-343 fall
; between them and are CDDL, not ABNF (`' .det rfc5234-core` closes one
; literal and `rfc5234-core = '` opens the next).  They are held as two
; regions for that reason and are never presented as one run.
;
; Source digest (sha256 of the full cached source text):
;   94f86116c04fde0f11d54576465181090ec33983d78db82527c0703a41976774
; Source: RFC 9165, "Additional Control Operators for the Concise
;         Data Definition Language (CDDL)", C. Bormann, December
;         2021, Standards Track, ISSN 2070-1721.
;         <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9165.txt>
; =====================================================================

; Section 3, fourth bullet.  The sentence that introduces it, quoted:
;
;      As is customary for ABNF, the syntax of ABNF itself (_not_ the
;      syntax expressed in ABNF!) is relaxed to allow a single line feed
;      as a newline:
; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM A-1 (source lines 298-298, sha256 cc16c384528205841ddb57b18cb42c32b4cf21a24a898f6be04367e13b44b97f) ----
      CRLF = %x0A / %x0D.0A
; ---- END VERBATIM A-1 ----

; Figure 3: An Example of Dedenting Concatenation - the controller of
; `"oid" .det cbor-tags-oid`, before dedenting.
; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM A-2 (source lines 211-214, sha256 87530aa2f70542db9656e6eef5da983debe70b8ba0a97376eab682515a8a8ed4) ----
     oid = 1*arc
     roid = *arc
     arc = [nlsb] %x00-7f
     nlsb = %x81-ff *%x80-ff
; ---- END VERBATIM A-2 ----

; Figure 5 - the rfc3339 rule-list, before dedenting.  Note that source
; lines 334 and 339 are genuinely EMPTY (zero width), not margin-indented,
; which is why Section 2.3's blank-line clause applies to them.
; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM A-3 (source lines 323-340, sha256 7c16060d81fa7b7175172deef5f2f6fbd0d34d66dbba971b8c22f4a9df0a892c) ----
      date-fullyear   = 4DIGIT
      date-month      = 2DIGIT  ; 01-12
      date-mday       = 2DIGIT  ; 01-28, 01-29, 01-30, 01-31 based on
                                ; month/year
      time-hour       = 2DIGIT  ; 00-23
      time-minute     = 2DIGIT  ; 00-59
      time-second     = 2DIGIT  ; 00-58, 00-59, 00-60 based on leap sec
                                ; rules
      time-secfrac    = "." 1*DIGIT
      time-numoffset  = ("+" / "-") time-hour ":" time-minute
      time-offset     = "Z" / time-numoffset

      partial-time    = time-hour ":" time-minute ":" time-second
                        [time-secfrac]
      full-date       = date-fullyear "-" date-month "-" date-mday
      full-time       = partial-time time-offset

      date-time       = full-date "T" full-time
; ---- END VERBATIM A-3 ----

; Figure 5 - the rfc5234-core rule-list, before dedenting.
; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM A-4 (source lines 344-345, sha256 b12abb4e76ad219b7050a008be406f4f2416b82c00c9f3986184e04981536c0a) ----
      DIGIT          =  %x30-39 ; 0-9
      ; abbreviated here
; ---- END VERBATIM A-4 ----
